A single-layer perceptron (SLP) forms the simplest neural network architecture. It consists of: 
 Input layer: This layer receives the input features. 
 Output layer: This layer produces the prediction. 
In the case of a binary classification problem, the perceptron outputs either a 0 or 1. The output layer is typically a single neuron that uses a 
